{"ts":"2026-07-28T14:04:06.683Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"45aa267ce86ee33cac29f976","agent_provenance":{"model":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-ay3l0p"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Nested pm test coverage changes repository-root fixtures because outer PM_PATH sandboxing leaks into package-owned run-tests"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Running node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage directly from the checkout passes all 381 files and 6,451 tests at 100/100/100/100. Linking the identical command through pm test fails 11 validate ownership/path-classification cases under schema context and the same cases plus merge-receipt context under tracker context. The outer linked-test runner replaces PM_PATH with a temporary schema or tracker copy; repository-root validation fixtures then derive ownership and path candidates from the copied tracker rather than the checkout, despite run-tests.mjs providing its own inner test sandboxes. This makes the documented package-owned sandbox runner unsafe to compose as a broad linked test and produces false product failures."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:cli","area:testing","context-integrity","developer-experience","sandbox"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-28T14:04:06.683Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-28T14:04:06.683Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Direct and pm-linked executions of node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage produce the same test and coverage result; No unit or integration test reads or writes the real repository .agents/pm tracker; Schema and tracker linked-test modes retain their documented semantics for genuine pm commands"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make package-owned test runners compositionally isolated when invoked through pm linked-test sandboxes"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"The same authoritative coverage command should have one result whether run directly or through PM evidence orchestration"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Prevents false coverage failures and lets broad gates be recorded as executable PM evidence without exposing the real tracker"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"run-tests.mjs derives repository fixtures from the checkout while every test PM read/write remains sandboxed, and a nested pm test regression proves parity"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"PR #795 exact-head verification produced repeatable direct-green/linked-red evidence in both schema and tracker modes"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-92if"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Package-owned coverage remains 100/100/100/100 under a linked PM run without repository-root fixture drift"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Direct coverage is green; schema and tracker linked contexts alter PM_PATH-derived ownership and path scans and fail otherwise-green tests"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"linked test sandbox composition"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/regression","value":false},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-7rlp","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-28T14:04:06.683Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-jd3m6p","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-07-28T14:04:06.683Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:de